    abstract = {This position paper provides insights aiming at resolving the most pressing needs and issues of computer vision algorithms. Specifically, these problemsrelatetothescarcityofdata, theinabilityofsuchalgorithms to adapt to never-seen-before conditions, and the challenge of developing explainable and trustworthy algorithms. This work proposes the incorporation of reasoning systems, and in particular of abductive reasoning, into image segmentation algorithms as a potential solution to the aforementioned issues.},
